* Right now we define a list of samples, then the same samples are used for all beam configurations.
  There is not option to switch off a specific sample from just one beam configuration.
  In NDSample.h, the kNDSample[kNNDSamples] array could become kNDSample[kNBeamConf][kNNDSamples] 

* The MC templates for CC samples are Ereco,yreco(,Etrue).
  This is reflected in variable names etc. Need to abtract this so that if we use different PDFs or
  MC templates (eg Ereco,Q^2(,Etrue)) then we are not stuck with inconsistent variable names.
  The abstraction should happen so that multiple definitions are allowed similtaneously (eg
  fit Ereco,yreco distribution for sample 1, but Epion distribution for sample 2).
  The lack of flexiility already shows up when adding NC samples (where yreco is not defined)
  and the fit only works because for all samples we have a coarse y binning (1 bin).

* Binning for MC templates - optimize

* In SDModel, adjust code so that it can read stored VALOR arrays in addition to VALOR DSTs.
  Then store the arrays in the repository. 
  Loose the ability to tweak the binning when running the default code checked out from the SVN repository.
  But DSTs too large to store in SVN.


